{"scenario": "S5", "step": "say", "message": "I just arrived in the UK and have no credit history", "attachment": false, "reply": "Welcome to the UK! Starting with a \"thin file\" (no credit history) is normal for newcomers [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)]. \n\nYour 6-month credit-building plan starts with foundational steps [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)]:\n1. **Proof of Address:** Keep your tenancy agreement or university letter handy [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n2. **UK Current Account:** Open a local bank account and use it regularly [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n3. **Electoral Roll / Residency:** Check if you can register to vote at your address; otherwise, provide proof of residency [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n4. **Phone Contract:** Move to a monthly mobile contract paid by direct debit [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n5. **Rent Reporting:** Consider having on-time rent payments reported to credit agencies [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n6. **Credit-Builder Card:** Apply for a starter credit card, use it for small purchases, and pay in full every month [KB: Credit-building basics (UK)].\n\nWould you like me to save this 6-month plan to your tracked tasks?\n\n_Illustrative general information - verify with your university, bank and official sources._", "cards": ["credit_plan", "sources"], "tools": ["get_credit_plan", "search_knowledge"], "provider": "gemini", "model": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "cached": true, "latency_ms": 312, "actions": []}
